# Inheritance

## `extends` — an "is-a" relationship

```java
public class SavingsAccount extends BankAccount {
    private double rate;
    public void addInterest() { balance += (long)(balance * rate); }
}
```

Gains the parent's fields & methods. Java = **single inheritance** (one superclass).

## `super` — reach the parent

```java
public SavingsAccount(long opening, double rate) {
    super(opening);      // parent constructor, first statement
    this.rate = rate;
}
```

- `super(...)` — parent constructor · `super.method()` — parent's version

## Override with `@Override`

- Same signature, new body; `@Override` makes the compiler check it
- **`final`** class → can't be extended; `final` method → can't be overridden
- Every chain of `extends` ends at **`Object`**
